1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,900
What if your research record had a Play button?
Built from public ORCID assertions.

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:19,900
Start from one public record.
A stored copy of a public ORCID record, labelled on screen. Everything is generated in your browser.

3
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:31,900
Your scientific trading card.
Every value on the card comes from an asserted field. It is a playful format, not a measure of merit or impact.

4
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:43,900
Honest about quiet years.
One cell per month of dated outputs. Undated outputs are noted, not placed, and gaps stay visible.

5
00:00:44,400 --> 00:00:57,900
A year in review, no invented numbers.
Every figure traces back to a field in the record. Counts describe activity, not quality or impact.

6
00:00:58,400 --> 00:01:05,900
Rediscover something you wrote.
A title drawn from the record itself.

7
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:20,900
Know what to fix, and why.
A scored rubric over the public record, with a concrete fix for each finding. It checks record metadata, not research quality.

8
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:33,900
Draft NIH, ERC or Horizon biosketches.
Pre-filled from asserted fields only. A draft, not an official funder form: review and complete it.

9
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:45,900
Take your data with you.
BibTeX, RIS, CSL JSON, Schema.org JSON-LD and Markdown. Biosketch JSON keeps per-field provenance.

10
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:54,900
Science Record Player · Publish or Play
